# ONBOARD — every key here is OPTIONAL.
#
# With no keys the prototype runs fully offline: character replies come from the
# deterministic grounded composer (same retrieval, same citations, no network)
# and voice uses the browser speech engine. The UI always states which tier is
# running — it never claims an integration it does not have.
#
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and restart the dev server to go live.

# --- ElevenLabs (voice) -------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Read by server/voiceProxy.mjs, which `npm run dev` starts
# alongside Vite. Deliberately NOT prefixed with VITE_, so Vite cannot inline
# it into the client bundle: the browser posts text to /api/voice/tts and this
# process adds the credential.
#
# Voice ids are NOT set here — they live per character in
# src/voice/voiceProfiles.ts, keyed off each character's `voiceProfileId`.
# The cast voices are community/shared-library voices, which need a Creator-tier
# key or above. On a Free key the proxy automatically degrades to each profile's
# premade `fallbackVoiceId`, so the app still speaks either way.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=sk_...
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_turbo_v2_5
# VOICE_PROXY_PORT=8787

# If the app is served from somewhere other than the Vite dev server, point it
# at the proxy explicitly (otherwise it uses the same-origin /api/voice).
# VITE_VOICE_PROXY_URL=https://your-api.example.com/api/voice

# DEPRECATED demo-only path: a browser-side ElevenLabs key. It works, it is
# labelled "ELEVENLABS · DIRECT" in the UI, and it puts your key in the client
# bundle. Use the proxy above instead.
# VITE_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# VITE_ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_turbo_v2_5

# --- Scene images + cinematic video (media server) ----------------------------
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Read by server/mediaServer.mjs, which `npm run dev` starts.
# Used at AUTHORING time from the Studio: scene images and keyframes
# (text-to-image), then ~5 s clips animated from those keyframes (Wan 2.2
# image-to-video), downloaded and stored under
# $ASSET_ROOT/company/episodes/<episode>/{backgrounds,videos}/.
# Without it, clips resolve to procedural previs and the UI says so.
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=
# REPLICATE_VIDEO_MODEL=wan-video/wan-2.2-i2v-fast
# REPLICATE_IMAGE_MODEL=black-forest-labs/flux-schnell
# ASSET_ROOT=storage
# MEDIA_SERVER_PORT=8788

# --- Language model -----------------------------------------------------------
# Powers character conversation, the AI coach, knowledge extraction and
# scenario generation. Browser-side keys are fine for a demo, never production;
# in production point VITE_LLM_PROXY_URL at your own server route instead.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# VITE_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# VITE_LLM_PROXY_URL=https://your-api.example.com/llm
